{"candidateAnswer":"The women's shelter and the cat rescue center on the east side of town.","evidence":"[D2:1 | 6:10 pm on 22 December, 2022] Maria: Hey John, been a few days since we chatted. In the meantime, I donated my old car to a homeless shelter I volunteer at yesterday. How's the campaign going? I'm keen to hearabout it.\n[D11:10 | 6:13 pm on 10 April, 2023] Maria: I recently gave a few talks at the homeless shelter I volunteer at. It was really fulfilling and I received lots of compliments from other volunteers. It was a great reminder about why connecting with and helping others is so important. And, I bought a cross necklace to feel closer to my faith- which has made me happy.\n[D17:12 | 11:51 am on 3 June, 2023] Maria: John, that's such a great idea! It gives the pup a loving home and teaches your kids important values. If you need any help, let me know! I just started volunteering at a local dog shelter once a month.","itemId":"urn:uuid:612d9a7b-0b80-5d6d-ba02-282f17b4be08","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:92c179a633ec530fdcc1fe31779129d1aa967ae68a540cc54be80243bdd1bbf6","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"What shelters does Maria volunteer at?","referenceAnswer":"The homeless shelter, the dog shelter","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"92c179a633ec530fdcc1fe31779129d1aa967ae68a540cc54be80243bdd1bbf6"}}]}